          "distinct": true,
          "id": "0f31636f3c54762d6479cc316453e7d14f11e327",
          "message": "feat(reason-el): CR7–CR9 concrete domains on the shared numeric tower (sq-pbz04.2.2) [FABLE-5] (#1434)\n\n* feat(reason-el): CR7-CR9 concrete domains on the shared numeric tower (sq-pbz04.2.2) [FABLE-5]\n\nOpt-in `cdomain` feature: faceted owl:onDatatype/owl:withRestrictions\nsatisfiability + DataHasValue/singleton-DataOneOf point ranges, decided\nEXACTLY on sparq_substrate::numeric (Dec i128 fixed-point — the EL\nreasoner's first genuine substrate adoption; no private numeric layer).\n\n- New src/cdomain.rs owns facet parsing, canonical NormRange, emptiness\n  (CR7: empty range -> d ⊑ ⊥, clash reaches classes via CR5) and\n  value-space containment (CR8/CR9: d1 ⊑ d2 Sub axioms threaded through\n  data existentials by the ordinary CR1/CR3/CR4) — classify.rs untouched.\n- Thin extract.rs hooks: candidates stay NON_EL-marked; only ranges\n  PROVEN supported are rescued in decode. Mixed-structure nodes refused\n  (LHS-strengthening guard). Unsupported facet/datatype/value => the\n  whole range defers to skipped_axioms — no guessed sat/unsat verdict.\n- Supported: xsd:decimal, xsd:integer + 12 derived integer types with\n  implicit bounds folded in; min/max{In,Ex}clusive; exact integer\n  tightening (integer (5,6) empty, decimal (5,6) not).\n- Deferred (honest): pattern/length/digit facets, float/double or\n  non-numeric bases/values, onDataRange, datatypeComplementOf,\n  ill-formed bounds, unalignable i128 comparisons.\n- Default build byte-identical (feature OFF; no sparq-substrate dep).\n- Tests: CR7 unsat/sat closure oracles with countermodel notes, CR8\n  containment + role-mismatch negatives, deferral matrix, idempotence;\n  mutation spot-checks run (4 mutants killed; 1 initial survivor fixed\n  by strengthening boundary-equality cases).\n- CI: new `opt-in sparq-reason-el (cdomain ...)` feature-matrix leg +\n  golden update; README + skills/inference/SKILL.md fragment tables.\n\n🤖 SPARQ agent\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(reason-el): close the cd_foreign_marker LHS-strengthening soundness hole (sq-pbz04.2.2) [FABLE-5]\n\nIndependent adversarial verification (Opus) empirically confirmed an\nunsound entailment: the cdomain strictness guard only refused the\nintersectionOf-family structure (onProperty/someValuesFrom/hasValue/\nintersectionOf/oneOf), NOT the other non-EL markers. A datatype-range\nnode ALSO carrying owl:unionOf / owl:allValuesFrom / owl:*Cardinality /\nowl:hasSelf / owl:onDataRange / owl:datatypeComplementOf was rescued as\nrange-ONLY, dropping that structure and STRENGTHENING an LHS axiom\n(derived G <= H against the countermodel C=D=empty, p(g)=5, g not in H).\n\nFix: track cd_foreign_marker (any non-EL marker other than onDatatype/\nwithRestrictions) during extraction and refuse such nodes in\nresolve_cdomain across ALL THREE rescue paths (faceted ranges, DataOneOf\npoints, DataHasValue restrictions) — the node falls through to the\nexisting counted non_el skip, exactly like the intersectionOf case.\nLegitimate pure-range / point paths are untouched.\n\nTests (all confirmed RED pre-fix): unionOf / allValuesFrom /\ndatatypeComplementOf refusal analogues + the threaded G-not-subsumed-H\nregression with the countermodel in the assertion message.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(reason-el): non-vacuous regression tests for DataHasValue/DataOneOf cd_foreign_marker guards (sq-pbz04.2.2) [SONNET-4.6]\n\nAdd two tests that kill the clean mutation survivors identified by the\nOpus adversarial re-verify on PR #1434:\n\n- `data_has_value_marked_node_is_refused_not_strengthened`: covers the\n  inline guard at extract.rs:451 (`!idx.cd_foreign_marker.contains(&n)`\n  in the DataHasValue `exists_points` filter).  A node carrying both\n  `owl:hasValue 5` and `owl:unionOf (:C :D)` must be refused (skipped),\n  never decoded as ∃p.{5}; the clean A2 axiom still chains {5} ⊆ [0,10]\n  into B.  Deleting line 451 → skipped_axioms drops to 0 and A wrongly\n  derives B → both assertions go RED.\n\n- `data_one_of_marked_node_is_refused_not_strengthened`: covers the\n  `cd_foreign_marker` branch inside `structure()` at extract.rs:412 (the\n  DataOneOf / singleton-literal oneOf path).  A node carrying both\n  `owl:oneOf (5)` and `owl:unionOf (:C :D)` in LHS position must be\n  refused; the clean F → ∃p.{5} → [0,10] → G chain is unaffected.\n  Deleting the cd_foreign_marker branch of structure() → the mixed node\n  enters `cd_range` and the axiom is decoded instead of skipped →\n  skipped_axioms drops to 0 → RED.\n\nMutation-kill proof run in-worktree; all 18 cdomain tests green in\ndefault / cdomain / all-features states; clippy -D warnings + rustdoc\nall-features clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
